{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1493579-mortal-the-morting-joke-splat","id":1493579,"title":"Mortal: The Morting, joke splat","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-23T08:56:25-07:00","id":1493579,"title":"Mortal: The Morting, joke splat","content":"Fun fan splat I created very quickly and just for the laughs. A parody of the CofD design philosophy, done lovingly as I've played every CofD gameline at least once. Hope you enjoy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Introduction:</b><br /> <br /> You always thought you were average. That all changed when you went to sleep one night. You didn't remember your dreams like normal, but unlike normal you realized... you are Mortal!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Character Types:</b><ul><li><b>Hot (Siren)</b> - You are attractive to some people, some of the time.</li> <li><b>Angry</b> <b>(Beast)</b> - You get angry at somethings, some of the time.</li> <li><b>Spiritual (Shaman)</b> - You feel one with the world, some of the time.</li> <li><b>Superstitious (Ghost Whisperer)</b> - You think you sometimes see ghosts, some of the time.</li> <li><b>Edgy (Goth)</b> - You like to be dark and mysterious, some of the time.</li> </ul><b>Faction Types:</b><ul><li><b>Old Fashioned</b> - This group likes things the way they were, some of the time.</li> <li><b>Innovators</b> - This groups likes it when things change, some of the time.</li> <li><b>Curious</b> - This group likes to uncover secrets, some of the time.</li> <li><b>Not Curious</b> - This group doesn't like to uncover secrets, some of the time.</li> <li><b>Ordinary</b> - This group believes they are the most normal out of all the other groups.</li> </ul><b>Template:</b><ul><li><b>Anchors</b> - Replace Virtue and Vice with Normal/Abnormal. Normal is what your character is normally known for, Abnormal is what your character is not known to normally do. Resolving either anchor as a minor setback regains 1 Willpower point, resolving either anchor as a major setback regains all Willpower points.</li> <li><b>Normalcy</b> - Replace Integrity with Normalcy. Instead of a 1-10 scale you calculate your Normalcy by 5 - your Presence + Composure. Whenever your character takes an action that isn't normal you take 1 minor Normalcy Damage (/), 1 major Normalcy damage(X), or 1 severe Normalcy damage(*) depending on the abnormality of the action. At full minor Normalcy damage, your character's Impression with Mortals drops by 1 to a minimum of average (does not affect mortals already hostile) as you are considered weird. At full major Normalcy damage, your character's Impression with Mortals drops by 2 to a minimum of hostile as you are now considered abnormal. At full severe Normalcy damage, you die of embarrassment like a Sims character.</li> <li><b>Abnormalities</b> - As you increase your Atypical stat you gain Abnormalities. These Abnormalities are when your character is too normal, to the extent that it creates an Uncanny Valley effect, such as teeth are too perfect or face is too symmetrical. Every Abnormality imposes a -1 Penalty to talking with Mortals, but grants 1 Dot of a Supernatural Merit.</li> <li><b>Power Stat</b> - You gain the Power Stat of Atypical that tracks from 1 to 10. At 5 Atypical The Benefits of Atypical is described below:<ul><li>1 - Attribute/Skill Max = 3.</li> <li>2 - Attribute/Skill Max = 4.</li> <li>3 - Attribute/Skill Max = 4.</li> <li>4 - Attribute/Skill Max = 5.</li> <li>5 - Attribute/Skill Max = 5. 1 Abnormality.</li> <li>6 - Attribute/Skill Max = 6. 1 Abnormality.</li> <li>7 - Attribute/Skill Max = 7. 2 Abnormalities.</li> <li>8 - Attribute/Skill Max = 8. 3 Abnormalities.</li> <li>9 - Attribute/Skill Max = 9. 4 Abnormalities.</li> <li>10 - Attribute/Skill Max = 10. 5 Abnormalities.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Normality Check</b> - If a character takes an action outside of being Normal they must make a Normality Check, Presence + Empathy.<ul><li><b>Critical Success</b> = That was the most normal thing you could do! Gain 1 Beat and heal the least farthest right Normalcy Damage your character has.</li> <li><b>Success</b> = That was pretty normal. Nothing happens.</li> <li><b>Failure</b> = You feel shame for not being normal. Gain the Guilty, Spooked, or Shaken Condition.</li> <li><b>Dramatic Failure</b> = You have failed to behave normally. Gain the Hunted Condition, a Rank 3 Angel is tracking you down because it thinks your not normal (and possibly a Demon), even though you are normal.</li> </ul></li> </ul><b>Experience Costs:</b><ul><li>Attribute = 4 XP</li> <li>Skill = 2 XP</li> <li>Skill Specialty = 1 XP</li> <li>Merit = 1 XP</li> <li>Atypical = 5 XP</li> </ul><b>Mortal Magic:</b><br /> <br /> Mortals do not start with access to magic or magic like abilities. That doesn't stop them from thinking they might have them. Some Mortals may think they have magical abilities, but the act of trying to use them is not normal and will result in a Normality Check.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-23T18:57:00-07:00","id":1493610,"title":"","content":"I really like using the additional rule found in page 72: &quot;All Mortals within a city must have Normality values according to a bell curve distribution, failure to do so will cause a character to undergo a Normality Check due to an abnormal distribution of Normality. Your character counts towards this distribution, meaning that their arrival or departure can cause cascading Normality Checks in NPCs, this is normally a problem&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}